          %h2#CriticalStringsAndQuantumAnomalies Critical string theories and quantum anomalies
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
            for the
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string"} string
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma+model"} sigma model
            in general has a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+anomaly"} quantum anomaly
            of both kinds:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                For both the bosonic string and the superstring the corresponding
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Polyakov+action"} Polyakov action
                has a
                %a{:href => ""} gauge anomaly
                for the
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+field+theory"} conformal symmetry
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
                of
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+space"} target space
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dilaton"} dilaton
                background field. For vanishing dilaton field this anomaly vanishes exactly for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo =
                      %mn 26
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = 26
                for the bosonic model, and in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo =
                      %mn 10
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = 10
                for the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring"} superstring
              %p
                For target spaces of these dimensions one speaks of
                = succeed "." do
                  %strong critical string theory
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-critical+string"} non-critical string
                models can and have been considered.
            %li
              %p
                Apart from the gauge anomaly, the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
                of the
                = succeed "-" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string"} string
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-model"} sigma-model
                also in general has an
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/quantum+anomaly#AnomalousActionFunctional"} anomalous action functional
                , for two reasons:
              %ol
                %li
                  %p
                    The
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holonomy"} higher holonomy
                    of the higher
                    = succeed "s" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/background+gauge+field"} background gauge field
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
                    of a
                    = succeed ";" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/line+bundle"} line bundle
                %li
                  %p
                    The fermionic
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+integral"} path integral
                    over the
                    = succeed "-" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldsheet"} worldsheet
                    = succeed "s" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spinor"} spinor
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring"} superstring
                    produces as section of a
                    = succeed "." do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pfaffian+line+bundle"} Pfaffian line bundle
              %p
                In order for the action functional to be well-defined, the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
                of these different anomaly
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/line+bundle"} line bundle
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+space"} configuration space
                must have trivial class (as
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle"} bundles with connection
              %ol
                %li
                  %p
                    For the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string"} heterotic string
                    (necessarily closed) the anomaly cancellation condition is known as the
                    %em
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+mechanism"} Green-Schwarz mechanism
                    \: it says that the background fields of
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
                    and
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-field"} B-field
                    must organize to a
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+differential+string+structure"} twisted differential string structure
                    whose twist is given by the background
                    = succeed "." do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+field"} Yang-Mills field
                %li
                  %p
                    For the open
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+string"} type II string
                    the condition is known as the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Freed-Witten+anomaly+cancellation"} Freed-Witten anomaly cancellation
                    condition: it says that the restriction of the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-field"} B-field
                    to any
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane"} D-brane
                    must consistute the twist of a
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+spin%5Ec+structure"} twisted spin^c structure
                    on the brane.
                  %p
                    A more detailed analysis of these type II anomalies is in (
                    %a{:href => "#DFMI"}> DFMI
                    ) and (
                    %a{:href => "#DFMII"}> DFMII
                    ).
                  %p
                    See also
                    = succeed "." do
                      %em
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diaconescu-Moore-Witten+anomaly"} Diaconescu-Moore-Witten anomaly
          %h2#subtopics Subtopics
          %h3#ingredients Ingredients
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-model"}> sigma-model
                ,
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+CFT"}> 2d CFT
                    ,
                    = succeed "," do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+SCFT"} 2d SCFT
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-spectral+triple"} 2-spectral triple
                  %ul
                    %li
