          %h3#scattering_amplitudes Scattering amplitudes
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S-matrix"} S-matrix
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Veneziano+amplitude"} Veneziano amplitude
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+scattering+amplitude"} string scattering amplitude
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-adic+string+theory"} p-adic string theory
          %h3#EllipticGenera
            Elliptic genera, elliptic cohomology and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi tmf
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} tmf
          %blockquote
            %p
              A properly developed theory of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+cohomology"} elliptic cohomology
              is likely to shed some light on what string theory really means. (
              %a{:href => "#Witten87"}> Witten 87, very last sentence
              )
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/large+volume+limit"} large volume limit
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partition+function"} partition function
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring"} superstring
            on a given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+space"} target
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+genus"} elliptic genus
            of that manifold (
            %a{:href => "#Witten87"}> Witten 87
            ), the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witten+genus"} Witten genus
            (see there for more).
          %p
            Since the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witten+genus"} Witten genus
            in turn is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/decategorification"} decategorification
            of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+orientation+of+tmf"} string orientation of tmf
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tmf"} tmf
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+%28Eilenberg-Steenrod%29+cohomology"} generalized (Eilenberg-Steenrod) cohomology
            classifies full string theories, in refinement of how the classification of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane+charge"} D-brane charge
            (just the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary+conditions"} boundary conditions
            for
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+strings"} open strings
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory"} K-theory
          %p
            A non-trivial conistency check of this idea is announced in (
            %a{:href => "#Nikolaus14"}> Nikolaus 14
            ).
          %h3#topological_strings Topological strings
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A-model"}> A-model
              ,
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-model"} B-model
          %h3#string_phenomenology String phenomenology
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+phenomenology"} string phenomenology
              %ul
                %li
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G%E2%82%82-MSSM"} G₂-MSSM
          %h3#string_theory_results_applied_elsewhere String theory results applied elsewhere
          %p
            Beyond the speculative hypothetized role of string theory as a theory behind observed
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/particle+physics"} particle physics
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/LHC"} LHC
          %p For more see
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory+results+applied+elsewhere"} string theory results applied elsewhere
          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p
            Suggestion to understand the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Veneziano+amplitude"} Veneziano amplitude
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+hadrodynamics"} quantum hadrodynamics
            as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scattering+amplitude"} scattering amplitude
            of chains of particles with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/harmonic+oscillator"} harmonic
            nearest-neighbour interaction, in the continuum limit described by the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Polyakov+action"} Polyakov action
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            (alongside
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Polyakov+gauge-string+duality"} Polyakov gauge-string duality
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leonard+Susskind"}> Leonard Susskind
              \:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Structure of Hadrons Implied by Duality
              %strong 1
              (1970) 1182 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevD.1.1182"}> doi:10.1103/PhysRevD.1.1182
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p Popular exposition:
          %ul
            %li#Green86
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Green"}> Michael Green
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Superstrings
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/24976036"} jstor:24976036
          %p
            Textbooks on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            (for more see at
            = succeed "):" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/books+about+string+theory"} books about string theory
          %ul
            %li#GreenSchwarzWitten88
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Green"}> Michael Green
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Schwarz"} John Schwarz
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} Edward Witten
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Superstring theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/250488"} spire:250488
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.cambridge.org/us/academic/subjects/physics/theoretical-physics-and-mathematical-physics/superstring-theory-25th-anniversary-edition-volume-1?format=HB&isbn=9781107029118"} ISBN:9781107029118
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/1384879"} spire:1384879
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9781139248570"} doi:10.1017/CBO9781139248570
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Duff"} Mike Duff
              %p
                %em>
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/The+World+in+Eleven+Dimensions"}> The World in Eleven Dimensions
                  \: Supergravity, Supermembranes and
                  = succeed "-theory" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi M
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
                ,
              %p
                IoP 1999 (
                %a{:href => "https://www.crcpress.com/The-World-in-Eleven-Dimensions-Supergravity-supermembranes-and-M-theory/Duff/9780750306720"}> publisher
                )
            %li#Polchinski01
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joseph+Polchinski"}> Joseph Polchinski
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/String+theory"} String theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Deligne"}> Pierre Deligne
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pavel+Etingof"} Pavel Etingof
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dan+Freed"} Dan Freed
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Kazhdan"} David Kazhdan
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Morgan"} John Morgan
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} Edward Witten
              %p
                %em>
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quantum+Fields+and+Strings"}> Quantum Fields and Strings
                  , A course for mathematicians
                , 2 vols. Amer. Math. Soc. Providence 1999. (
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.ias.edu/qft"}> web version
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Katrin+Becker"}> Katrin Becker
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Melanie+Becker"} Melanie Becker
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Schwarz"} John Schwarz
              %p
                %em> String Theory and M-Theory: A Modern Introduction
                ,
              %p Cambridge University Press (2006)
              %p
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511816086"}> doi:10.1017/CBO9780511816086
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://nucleares.unam.mx/~alberto/apuntes/bbs.pdf"} pdf
            %li
