            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
                ,
              %p
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Introduction+to+Higher+Supergeometry"} Introduction to Higher Supergeometry
              %p
                Lectures at
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://www.maths.dur.ac.uk/lms/109/index.html"} Higher Structures in M-Theory, LMS-EPSRC Durham Symposium, August 2018
          %h3#more_technical_details More technical details
          %h4#gut GUT
          %p
            A key article for the idea that string theory provides a framework for realistic (chiral)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/grand+unified+theories"} grand unified theories
            combined with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+gravity"} quantum gravity
            was
          %ul
            %li#Witten84
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Some properties of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi O
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 32
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(32)
                  superstrings
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Witten84.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            based on the insights of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+anomaly+cancellation"} Green-Schwarz anomaly cancellation
          %h4#elliptic_genera_elliptic_homology_and_tmf Elliptic genera, elliptic homology and tmf
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partition+function"} partition function
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring"} superstring
            was understood to be an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+genus"} elliptic genus
            (the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witten+genus"} Witten genus
          %ul
            %li#Witten87
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
              ,
              %em Elliptic Genera And Quantum Field Theory
              , Commun.Math.Phys. 109 525 (1987) (
              %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.cmp/1104117076"}> Euclid
              )
          %p
            A nontrivial consistency check on the suggestion that this means that string backgrounds are classified in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tmf"} tmf
            is given in
          %ul
            %li#Nikolaus14
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Nikolaus"}> Thomas Nikolaus
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/T-Duality+in+K-theory+and+Elliptic+Cohomology"} T-Duality in K-theory and Elliptic Cohomology
              = succeed "," do
                %em String Geometry Network Meeting
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.ingvet.kau.se/juerfuch/conf/esi14/esi14_34.html"} website
          %h4#quantum_anomalies Quantum anomalies
          %p
            Discussion of type II
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+anomalies"} quantum anomalies
            is in
          %ul
            %li#DFMI
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacques+Distler"}> Jacques Distler
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dan+Freed"} Dan Freed
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Greg+Moore"} Greg Moore
                %em Orientifold Précis
                in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
                (eds.)
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Mathematical+Foundations+of+Quantum+Field+and+Perturbative+String+Theory"} Mathematical Foundations of Quantum Field and Perturbative String Theory
                Proceedings of Symposia in Pure Mathematics, AMS (2011) (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0906.0795"}> arXiv
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.ma.utexas.edu/users/dafr/bilbao.pdf"} slides
            %li#DFMII
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacques+Distler"}> Jacques Distler
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dan+Freed"} Dan Freed
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Greg+Moore"} Greg Moore
                %em Spin structures and superstrings
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1007.4581"}> arXiv:1007.4581
                )
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring"} superstring
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbation+theory"} perturbation theory
            (see at
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+scattering+amplitudes"} string scattering amplitudes
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
              ,
              %em Superstring Perturbation Theory Revisited
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1209.5461"}> arXiv:1209.5461
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %h3#FieldMedalWork Fields medal (and other) work related to string theory
          %p
            Pure
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematics"} mathematics
            work which is closely related string theory and was awarded with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fields+medal"} Fields medal
            includes the following.
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+Borcherds"}> Richard Borcherds
            , 1998
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertex+algebras"} vertex algebras
              %ul
                %li
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monster+vertex+algebra"}> monster vertex algebra
                  ,
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Goddard-Thorn+theorem"} Goddard-Thorn theorem
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maxim+Kontsevich"}> Maxim Kontsevich
            , 1998
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homological+mirror+symmetry"}> homological mirror symmetry
                ,
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gromov-Witten+theory"} Gromov-Witten theory
            %li
              %p
